{"name":"Dead Pixel","hex":"#3b3a3a","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dead pixel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pixel on an LCD that does not light up.","a miscolored pixel on an image where it is otherwise not intended to be."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dead_pixel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Defective pixel","blocks":[{"text":"A defective pixel or a dead pixel is a pixel on a liquid crystal display (LCD) that is not functioning properly. The ISO standard ISO 13406-2 distinguishes between three different types of defective pixels, while hardware companies tend to have further distinguishing types."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/20/Lcd_display_dead_pixel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Defective_pixel"},{"title":"Pixel","blocks":[{"text":"In digital imaging, a pixel, pel, or picture element is the smallest addressable element of a raster image. In a display device, dot matrix printer, or ASCII art a pixel is the smallest element whose output can generally be controlled independently."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Pixel-example.png/330px-Pixel-example.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pixel"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/20/Lcd_display_dead_pixel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/20/Lcd_display_dead_pixel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Close-up of an LCD, showing a dead green subpixel as a black rectangle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALcd_display_dead_pixel.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Damaged_photo_sensitive_chip.